  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the given problem as the following product:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%\\times 14=35\n$$\n\nUsing the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,%=35÷14=\\frac{35}{14}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{14}=\\frac{35÷7}{14÷7}=\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5\\times 50}{2\\times 50}=\\frac{250}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{250}{100}=250%\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
